TASK-229 runtime harness: the Peek's hover card. Temporary code, never
committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task229-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # Fixture pages on http://127.0.0.1:8229/: host.html, pinhost.html,
    # favhost.html, other.html (untitled hosts) and peek1-3.html, each with a
    # <title> and a <link rel=icon> PNG (a Peek without a favicon has no badge).
    OUT="$PWD/.derived-logs/task229"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify229 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=1 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for "done" in $OUT/verify-1.log (about 70 s), kill that pid, then the
    # same with DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=2 (the relaunch, about 20 s). Phase 3
    # (split rows, splitl/splitr.html and peek4/5.html) runs on a fresh data dir.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task229-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Phase 1 opens a Peek over a normal tab, a tab then pinned and a tab then
favourited, leaving each so the host and the Peek are pictured. In light then
dark it hovers the normal row's body (host card), moves onto the badge (Peek
card), moves back; enters the pinned row straight onto the badge; enters the
favourite tile on its chip, then moves to its middle. Then it sleeps the
normal host (parked Peek) and hovers its badge, and selects the host (Peek
presented, no picture) and hovers its badge. Phase 2 relaunches and hovers
the restored hosts' badges (only peekURL left). Hover goes through the views'
own mouseEntered / mouseMoved / mouseExited; a 120 Hz sampler logs show and
hide times.

Results (2026-10-28, screen locked, so no window captures; cacheDisplay and
layer.render of the glass card come out blank): the badge swapped the row's
card for the Peek's 0.04 s after the move, and back, in light and dark; fresh
hovers on a pinned badge or a tile chip waited 0.46 s; every card's top was
level with its row and 6 pt outside the sidebar; live Peeks showed their own
title, URL and picture (normal, pinned, favourite); the parked Peek kept its
title and picture; the selected host's Peek card had no picture; restored
Peeks (normal and pinned) showed the URL alone in a 38 pt card. The favourite
came back dormant after the relaunch (the harness favourited a tab that also
stayed in the tab list), so its tile had no badge and showed the tile's card.

Phase 3 (2026-10-29, split rows, screen locked): a Peek over each of two
tabs, then the two split. Light and dark: each pane's title area showed its
pane's card and each pane's badge its Peek's card, every move swapping at
once (0.04-0.05 s), badge to badge included. Layout in a 188 pt cell: left
title, left close button (hover), 4 pt, left badge, 14 pt, divider, 14 pt,
right favicon, right title, close button, 4 pt, right badge, 4 pt; nothing
overlapped. The left title had 32 pt at rest (52 pt without the badge).
Clearing the left pane's Peek hid its badge, and its area then showed the
pane's own card.

TASK-230 re-run (2026-10-29, phases 1 and 2, screen locked; logThumbnails
lists, per host, whether the host's and its Peek's files exist): before
quitting the normal and pinned hosts' Peeks had files under their derived
keys; after the relaunch both keys were still live and hovering the
restored badges showed the picture from disk (normal in light, pinned in
dark) in a 208 pt card. The favourite's Peek had no file under the
favourite's key because the harness favourited the tab after it was
pictured (the next capture writes the new key, as for any re-keyed row).

